## Why This Is Asked
Tests lock-free design, ABA avoidance with sequence counters, memory ordering, and NUMA-aware reclamation strategies.

## Key Concepts
- Lock-free queues with sequence counters
- Epoch-based memory reclamation
- NUMA locality and cache-line padding
- Memory order: acquire/release and fences
- Batch enqueues to reduce barrier overhead

## Code Example
```cpp
// Pseudo-enqueue (simplified)
struct Slot { uint64_t seq; char data[128]; };
Slot ring[N];
_Atomic uint64_t head=0, tail=0;
void enqueue(void* msg){
  uint64_t pos = atomic_fetch_add(&tail, 1);
  Slot& s = ring[pos & (N-1)];
  while (s.seq != pos) _mm_pause();
  memcpy(s.data, msg, 128);
  atomic_store_explicit(&s.seq, pos+1, memory_order_release);
}
```

